{
  "slug": "artist:krs-one",
  "name": "KRS-One",
  "editorial_article": "Born Lawrence Parker in 1965, the Bronx-based MC first gained national prominence in 1987 as the lead voice of Boogie Down Productions on the seminal album Criminal Minded. Following the murder of his partner DJ Scott La Rock later that year, he pivoted toward the socially conscious lyricism that defined his 1988 follow-up By All Means Necessary. His 1993 solo debut Return of the Boom Bap featured production from DJ Premier and Showbiz, the latter contributing the enduring single Sound of da Police. Throughout the 1990s, he balanced mainstream commercial successes like the number three Billboard 200 album I Got Next with militant activism, notably establishing the Stop the Violence Movement to address regional tensions. His 2009 collaborative project with Buckshot, Survival Skills, debuted at number 62 on the Billboard 200, receiving praise for its uncompromising production and lyrical chemistry.",
